  A FAIL here predicts a FAIL of the same test in every host: it is a
  plugin-side alignment result, not a host compatibility one. Read the
  'best null at +N' column before blaming the DSP — a deep null at a
  non-zero N means the audio is fine and the LATENCY REPORT is short
  by N samples, which is a one-line fix and a different bug entirely.
